-- AMM ADAPTATION -- wCELO -- STEP 2 CONTROL-EVENT DIAGNOSTIC
-- This is an additional diagnostic, not a detector or a change to its rules.
-- Source: 12D_wcelo_matched_control_pool_raw_swaps.csv
-- Source MD5: 59f9477140f4dbb90a81b1e10dbd814d
-- Requests: 33 exceptional transactions (original rows 2-34), plus rows 1 and 35.
-- All requests are within the previously agreed historical observation interval.
-- The one-day filter reduces scanning to the day containing these 35 transactions.
-- We retrieve ALL logs in each requested transaction, including Transfer/Sync/Swap.
-- This uses the ethereum.logs retrieval pattern used for ECO-USDT Stage 3.
-- Documentation: https://docs.dune.com/data-catalog/evm/ethereum/decoded/event-logs
-- Raw hex and quoted original quantities preserve exact integer values.
-- No rows are removed from the original sample; no amounts are netted.
-- Query results may clarify the pattern but do not prove its economic cause.
--
-- HOW TO USE
-- Paste this entire SQL into a new Dune query and run it once.
-- Download the complete CSV (not only a displayed preview).
-- Save in Data/cleaned as:
-- amm_adaptation_additional_pool_wcelo_output_control_pool_step2_nonstandard_swap_diagnostic.csv
-- NEXT STEP: inspect coverage and compare the saved Swap fields with raw logs,
-- then examine transfer evidence before any methodological decision.
